.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-restore-raw-volume 1  "tapectl-restore-raw-volume " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-restore\-raw\-volume \- Dump every file off a tape verbatim, using only what is on the tape itself (no database needed) — the emergency/heir path
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl restore raw\-volume\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-to\fR> [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dump every file off a tape verbatim, using only what is on the tape itself (no database needed) — the emergency/heir path
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR [default: /dev/nst0]
Tape device
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Destination directory
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Refuse unless the tape\*(Aqs own reported label matches (wrong\-tape guard) — not a database lookup
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
